Subject: [PATCH 140/230] perf(feed): skip offscreen card work; hard bundle
 budget in CI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The feed renders every matchday card eagerly even on a 360px phone:
content-visibility:auto with a reserved footprint (contain-intrinsic-
size) defers layout and paint of cards below the fold without moving
scrollbars, which is the free version of virtualization for a list of
uniform-height rows.

And because desktop dev hides what the fleet feels like, a budget
gate now runs after every build: gzip'd JS total <=200KB, biggest
chunk <=60KB, CSS total <=20KB (baseline ~146KB/50.8KB/10.9KB, so
real headroom before CI starts blocking rather than nagging).

